    {
      "id": "ascetic_purge",
      "name": "Ascetic / deck-thinning",
      "description": "burn the chaff - cards that thin your deck toward a lean engine (permanent deck-thinning). Two shapes: a strong, over-statted skill or attack carries the flag-op `{\"op\":\"purge\"}` so that playing it removes THAT card from your RUN DECK for the rest of the run (a stronger `exhaust` that never returns; you spend the card once, so over-stat it for its cost); OR the op `{\"op\":\"purge_card\"}` lets the PLAYER choose a card in hand and purge THAT one (targeted thinning - cut a Basic, Curse, or dead draw), and since the purge_card card itself stays it can be a normal repeatable skill. Pair with a deck the player WANTS thin (a few key payoff cards you dig to). THE PAYOFF for going small: a thin deck empties its draw pile fast, so gate a Grand-Finale-style finisher behind `when:{\"kind\":\"draw_pile_empty\"}` - a splashy over-printed effect that only fires once the whole deck has been drawn (the balance pass prices the gate in, so print BIG base-game-Grand-Finale numbers on it). One such finisher rewards the whole thinning plan; it is a payoff condition, not an identity of its own. Neither purge op goes on a basic; keep deck-thinning to 1-3 cards per class - it sharpens the identity, it isn't the whole identity. (`purge` is also mutually exclusive with `exhaust`.)",
      "metaphors": [
