      "description": "churn your hand - discard as fuel, cards that reward being thrown away (the base-game Reflex feel). Three tools: forced discard (random, or the player's choice) as a cheap enabler that pairs with draw; on-discard fuel cards that grant nothing when played but fire when THEY are discarded by an effect, so the player keeps them in hand and pitches them for value; and scry, which looks at the top few cards of the draw pile and discards any of them - a draw filter that also lets the player choose which fuel card to pitch, since a scry-discard counts as an effect-discard. Retrieving a card from the discard pile closes the loop. Ship discard income, a couple of on-discard fuel cards, and a scry/churn engine.",
      "metaphors": [
